INT. FEDERAL COURTROOM 11 - DAY

Oak paneling. A seal on the wall. A jury box with twelve empty chairs. It is a pretrial conference, and the room has the hush of a library.

JUDGE ROSALIND ABERNATHY-KOMOLAFE (60s, robe, reading glasses) presides. At the plaintiff's table: COUNSEL BENEDICT ASANTE-FAIRWEATHER (50s, three-piece suit) and his associate, MS. PRISCILLA DUARTE-LINDQVIST (20s, legal pad, nervous knee). At the defense table: ATTORNEY MARCUS OYELOWO-STRAND (40s, rolled sleeves) and his co-counsel, A WOMAN IN A NAVY SUIT (30s), who has not been introduced. The court reporter, DELPHINA MWANGI-HOLCOMB (50s), types without looking up.

JUDGE ROSALIND
Counsel, the pretrial order states discovery closed March first.

BENEDICT
It did, Your Honor.

MARCUS
It did not.

JUDGE ROSALIND
Mr. Oyelowo-Strand?

MARCUS
Your Honor, the plaintiff's production of the August emails came forty days late.

BENEDICT
Because your client's servers were corrupted.

MARCUS
Because your client's counsel was unreachable.

PRISCILLA
(whispering to Benedict)
That's not what the file says.

BENEDICT
(whispering back)
I know.

JUDGE ROSALIND
Counsel, address the court, not each other.

BENEDICT
Yes, Your Honor.

The woman in the navy suit leans toward Marcus and passes a folded note. He reads it. His jaw tightens.

MARCUS
Your Honor, with the court's permission, may I introduce my co-counsel?

JUDGE ROSALIND
Please.

THE WOMAN
(rising)
Jocasta Reyes-Abiola, Your Honor. Appearing for the defense.

JOCASTA
(to the room)
We have a motion.

Priscilla stops writing. Benedict removes his glasses. Delphina's fingers pause over the keys.

JUDGE ROSALIND
Ms. Reyes-Abiola, proceed.

JOCASTA
We move to compel the original server logs from August fourteenth.

BENEDICT
Your Honor, those logs do not exist.

JOCASTA
Then Mr. Asante-Fairweather can explain to the court why his firm billed us for reviewing them.

Silence. Priscilla, very softly, to no one:

PRISCILLA
Oh no.

Benedict sets down his pen and does not look at her.

JUDGE ROSALIND
Mr. Asante-Fairweather, would you care to respond?

BENEDICT
(slowly)
I would like a recess, Your Honor.

JUDGE ROSALIND
Denied. Respond.
